# Changelog

All notable changes to `hostnamed` are documented in this file, derived from the project's git history.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-10-14

### Changed (build / compatibility)
- **polkit is now a hard build dependency.** The `-Dpolkit=disabled` / `polkit` feature option has been removed, along with the unused `HAVE_POLKIT` define and every `polkit_found` conditional in the meson files. Previously a build without polkit failed at `#include <polkit/polkit.h>` anyway, and without polkit nothing could authorise the Set* methods. Anyone passing `-Dpolkit=...` to `meson setup` must drop it.
- Hostname validation (`SetHostname`, `SetStaticHostname`) is now strict RFC 1123: labels of 1-63 characters, no empty labels (`a..b`), no leading/trailing dot, and no label that starts or ends with `-`. Names that were previously accepted but are invalid under these rules are now rejected with `InvalidArgs`.
- `GetProductUUID` now returns the 16 raw UUID bytes (as systemd-hostnamed does) instead of the 36-character ASCII string as `ay`. It returns a `NotFound` error, rather than an empty array, when the UUID is unreadable, malformed, or the all-zero / all-0xFF placeholder.

### Fixed
- Fixed bogus `PropertiesChanged` emissions: `Chassis` and `IconName` were blanked and re-set on every resync, producing duplicate dict keys and a signal on every inotify event. The effective value (machine-info, then fallbacks) is now computed first and updated once; three file touches now produce one signal instead of ten.
- `IconName` is now derived from the effective chassis string, so `CHASSIS=laptop` in `/etc/machine-info` without an `ICON_NAME` yields `computer-laptop` rather than `computer`.
- `DefaultHostname` is now populated (`DEFAULT_HOSTNAME` from os-release, else `localhost`); it was always empty.
- `HostnameSource` can now report `default` (static hostname unset and kernel hostname unset, `(none)`, or equal to the default); it previously only ever reported `static` or `transient`.
- `SetPrettyHostname` no longer truncates arbitrary labels at the first dot. The leading-label reduction now applies only when the whole value is a valid hostname, so `Bob's PC v2.0` is stored as given while `dair.example.net` still becomes `dair`.
- Polkit challenges are now reported as `org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InteractiveAuthorizationRequired` when the caller passed `interactive=false` but authentication is possible, instead of a generic `AUTH_FAILED`, so GUI clients can retry with an agent dialog (matches localed).

### Added
- Device-tree fallbacks for platforms without DMI (ARM, RISC-V, e.g. Raspberry Pi): `HardwareModel` from `/sys/firmware/devicetree/base/model`, `HardwareVendor` from the vendor prefix of the first `compatible` entry, and `Chassis` from `chassis-type` when it is a known value.
- `HardwareVendor` is now taken from DMI `sys_vendor`, then `board_vendor`, then the device tree; `HardwareModel` from `product_name`, then `board_name`, then the device tree. Empty values and the unfilled template strings firmware leaves behind (`System manufacturer`, `System Product Name`, `To Be Filled By O.E.M.`, `Default string`, ...) are skipped at each step, so boards such as the ASUS PRIME B550-PLUS now report the real board name and vendor instead of the placeholder. `slack/hostnamectl` uses the same logic and the same placeholder list (it now also reads the device tree and honours `DMI_DIR` / `DT_DIR` for testing).
- `GetHardwareSerial` now returns the first usable serial from DMI `product_serial`, `board_serial`, `chassis_serial` (it previously read `chassis_serial` only, which many boards leave as `Default string`), skipping the same placeholder values, and falls back to the device-tree `serial-number` property on platforms without a DMI serial (e.g. Raspberry Pi).
- Expanded chassis table: rack-mount, multi-system and blade types map to `server`; IoT gateway and embedded PC map to `embedded`; all-in-one, pizza-box, space-saving, lunch-box, sealed-case, mini-PC and stick-PC map to `desktop`. The case tables in `slack/hostnamectl` were updated to match.

## [0.2.7.1] - 2026-06-27 to 2026-09-01
- Added validation for hostname metadata values and corrected the machine-info path constant.
- Man pages for `hostnamed(8)` and `hostnamectl(1)` added and compressed in the SlackBuild.
- New and updated translations (Arabic Latin script, Indonesian, Estonian and others) via Weblate; project version bumped to 0.2.7 then 0.2.7.1.
- Removed `sbindir` paths from the build.

## [0.2.6] - 2026-06-20

### Security
- Fixed a polkit authorization bypass and a JSON escaping bug in the D-Bus interface (PR #1, rizitis/main) (`9acb293`, `96438ab`)
- Reworked polkit authorization checks to run **asynchronously** via `PolkitAuthority` callbacks instead of blocking sync calls, so the agent password dialog no longer stalls the single-threaded main loop (`8afc587`)
- Added two dedicated polkit actions, `org.freedesktop.hostname1.get-product-uuid` and `org.freedesktop.hostname1.get-hardware-serial`, replacing reuse of the `set-hostname` action for hardware reads (`8afc587`)
- Added defence-in-depth value validation directly in the machine-info writer (`write_machine_info_key`), independent of caller-side checks (`8afc587`)

### Changed
- Cleaned up `hostnamed.SlackBuild`, removing leftover `localectl` references (`2154cfb`)
- Reworked hostname/machine-info file path references and added dedicated config options for `os-release` and `machine-info` paths (`ae6c851`, `e61b73e`, `1d59143`, `df1b9a4`)
- Added direct property-cache updates for machine-info keys, correctly emitting `PropertiesChanged` instead of relying on a full resync (`ea8a974`)
- Implemented a pretty-hostname sanitiser to derive a clean label from an FQDN (`b1c9527`)
- Refactored the polkit `.rules.in` logic for hostname management (`68c91f7`, `38ddd77`)

### Added
- Added GPLv2 license file (`de0dd36`)

## [0.2.0] - 2026-06-19
- Bumped version 0.1.0 → 0.2.0 (`3a072dc`)

## [0.1.0] - 2026-05-31 to 2026-06-17

### Added
- Initial project scaffolding: `main.c`, `rcl-hostname.c`/`.h`, `meson.build`, `meson_options.txt`, `README.md`, `LINGUAS`, `POTFILES` (`0056f42`, `233e8cf`, `ac4da26`, `952f142`, `2184bd5`)
- D-Bus interface description (`org.freedesktop.hostname1.xml`), service activation file (`.service.in`), polkit policy (`.policy`), and polkit rules (later templated as `.rules.in`) (`02fe5db`, `94dbb9e`, `64f6dc4`, `d630173`, `5251a8a`)
- SlackBuild packaging script (`2f36c95`), briefly renamed to `slack-desc` then restored (`db3bf5c`)
- `hostnamectl` and `localectl` companion shell scripts (`a3ed2a8`, `581d92b`)
- Input validation for hostnames and machine-info values (`65c0675`)
- `default_hostname`, privileged-group, and hostname-file configuration options (`d14df64`, `09b8666`)

### Changed
- Refactored authorization handling in `rcl-hostname.c` (`173a8b8`)
- Changed `FirmwareDate` D-Bus property type to `t` (uint64) and implemented microsecond-since-epoch parsing (`e5c2bc2`)
- Refactored the `RclState` structure and logging mechanism (`51c7a00`)
- Tightened the D-Bus security policy in `org.freedesktop.hostname1.conf`, replacing explanatory comments with explicit interface allow-rules (`47e7cce`)
- Simplified the polkit rule, removing an unneeded early return for non-privileged subjects (`fa2e743`)
- Refactored `hostnamectl` for clearer structure and parsing (`dff42ce`)
- Replaced decorative comment banners with plain separators across the codebase (`19e98c1`)
- Cleaned up and reformatted `meson.build` / `meson_options.txt` across several passes, removing dead/commented sections (`616ede9`, `be0bb13`, `4c03939`, `e4648f2`, `15de2e1`)
- Updated copyright year and author metadata in `rcl-hostname.c` (`8205b67`)
- Numerous incremental updates to `main.c`, `rcl-hostname.h`, and `meson.build` while stabilizing the initial build (`1ee763e`, `dbbd846`, `5a52b7c`, `7bfa26d`, `59f6673`, `661a430`, `30e4ff1`, `51cdd55`, `86a343c`, `f04035b`, `e4b5d9d`, `2a8e080`, `c3e4bfe`, `017e1c3`, `e3ad6e5`, `1574abd`)

### Removed
- Deleted and recreated `hostnamectl` during early iteration (`9dd6682`, `30a0201`, `6d92e35`)
